      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "title": "Sampling spec",
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Pika H3 Flex — sampling (official, do not change)\n\n| setting | value |\n|---|---|\n| sampler | `lcm` |\n| cfg | **1.0** (implicit — `BasicGuider` has no cfg input) |\n| sigmas | `ManualSigmas` = `1.0, 0.972973, 0.923077, 0.8, 0.571429, 0.333333, 0.0` |\n| steps | **6** (7 sigma values, trailing `0.0` is the terminator) |\n| LoRA strength | **1.0** (`LoraLoaderModelOnly`) |\n| size | 1344 x 768 |\n| length | 124 frames @ 24 fps (~5.2 s) |\n\n### Rules\n1. **Do NOT add a turbo / lightning / 4-step LoRA.** The Pika adapter is already distilled; stacking a speed LoRA breaks it and produces grid noise or collapsed structure.\n2. **Do NOT replace `ManualSigmas` with `BasicScheduler`.** The sigma list is hand-picked by Pika; no `scheduler` name reproduces it.\n3. The alpha is folded into `lora_B` and the scale is baked in, so `LoraLoaderModelOnly` strength must stay **1.0**.\n4. Keep `ref_image_size` = `match` for speed (`max` is several times slower).\n"
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "## Pika H3 Flex — sampling (official, do not change)\n\n| setting | value |\n|---|---|\n| sampler | `lcm` |\n| cfg | **1.0** (implicit — `BasicGuider` has no cfg input) |\n| sigmas | `ManualSigmas` = `1.0, 0.972973, 0.923077, 0.8, 0.571429, 0.333333, 0.0` |\n| steps | **6** (7 sigma values, trailing `0.0` is the terminator) |\n| LoRA strength | **1.0** (`LoraLoaderModelOnly`) |\n| size | 1344 x 768 |\n| length | 124 frames @ 24 fps (~5.2 s) |\n\n### Rules\n1. **Do NOT add a turbo / lightning / 4-step LoRA.** The Pika adapter is already distilled; stacking a speed LoRA breaks it and produces grid noise or collapsed structure.\n2. **Do NOT replace `ManualSigmas` with `BasicScheduler`.** The sigma list is hand-picked by Pika; no `scheduler` name reproduces it.\n3. The alpha is folded into `lora_B` and the scale is baked in, so `LoraLoaderModelOnly` strength must stay **1.0**.\n4. Keep `ref_image_size` = `match` for speed (`max` is several times slower).\n"
      }
    },
